Rule 1 (integer axis must be within the valid index range for x to avoid out-of-range gather)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= (0 - ndim(v_1)) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 2 (tuple axes: each axis must be within the valid index range for x to avoid out-of-range gather)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : (0 - ndim(v_1)) ≤ v_2[i] ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (tuple axes length cannot exceed the rank of x)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1)
